<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiang Army</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xiang Army was a regional military force raised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunan">Hunan</a> province by the scholar-official <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeng-guofan">Zeng Guofan</a> to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion</a>. Its success, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-hongzhang">Li Hongzhang</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huai-army">Huai Army</a>, was crucial in suppressing the Taiping. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> profile notes that this reliance on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-chinese">Han Chinese</a> regional armies transferred real military power away from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> court, weakening the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xiang-army.jpg" alt="Xiang Army" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The-Xiang-Army.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
